{"kind":"request","text":"CB-2: a celld room archives to a repository.\n\nThe fact at main 4cef11d2. A celld Worker has no archive provider.\n`apps/room/celld/wrangler.json` has no `ARTIFACTS` binding, and\ncelld does not offer Cloudflare Artifacts. `github-host.ts:82`\nstates \"No production archive mint\", and it exposes only\n`fixtureArchive(ports)`. So a celld room of the `base` family can\nrecord `bind-archive`, and no bytes leave the machine.\n\nScene: the owner of a `base` room on a Mac fleet founded the room\nwith `--host none`. The owner binds a GitHub repository, and then\nsends `bind-archive`. The room archives its journals to the\nrepository. `dap clone \u003cdir\u003e --archive` and `artroom-replay --all\n--expect-journals N --json` pass, with N from a separate list of\nscopes.\n\nFirst act, before any source: a design proposal.\n1. The provider, and why this one.\n2. Each credential that it holds, who holds it, and its lifetime.\n   The room's owner holds the credentials of the room's repository.\n3. What leaves the machine, and what decides it.\n4. What the driver of AE-1 needs from the provider, as a list of\n   functions.\nNo fixture port, no stand-in binding and no new Git service enters\nthe scene.\n\nNeeds: AE-1 and CB-1 on main. Order: after the stable base. Review\nby the checker with the Security conclusion.","body":{"conditions":"Planner accepts the design proposal on the provider; a base room on a Mac fleet founded with host none binds a GitHub repository and archives to it; dap clone --archive and artroom-replay --all pass with an independent journal count; gate passes; checker reviews with the Security conclusion","target_head":"4cef11d2783efaa591fac197d9a2ba093004456e","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}